# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate declares a reference mode occupation; an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gate rotates the single-particle basis. Placed back to back, the two gates prepare a *Slater determinant*; the modes start in the reference determinant and are then rotated into the target orbitals. The [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate captures that composition, and because it carries the reference occupation, transpiling it can use the rectangular [`givens_decomposition_slater()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/linalg-givens-decomposition-slater#qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater \"qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater\"), which realizes only the *occupied* orbitals, instead of the full square decomposition an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") alone requires. That is a strictly cheaper synthesis (see the payoff at the end of this guide).\n"
msgstr "Un gate [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") dichiara un'occupazione dei modi di riferimento; un gate [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") ruota la base di singola particella. Posti uno dopo l'altro, i due gate preparano un *determinante di Slater*; i modi partono dal determinante di riferimento e vengono poi ruotati negli orbitali di destinazione. Il gate [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") cattura questa composizione e, poiché porta con sé l'occupazione di riferimento, la sua transpilazione può usare la [`givens_decomposition_slater()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/linalg-givens-decomposition-slater#qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater \"qiskit_fermions.linalg.givens_decomposition_slater\") rettangolare, che realizza solo gli orbitali *occupati*, invece della decomposizione quadrata completa richiesta da un solo [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\"). Si tratta di una sintesi strettamente più economica (vedi il vantaggio alla fine di questa guida).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") transpiler pass detects the [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\")-then-[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") pattern in a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") and rewrites it into [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gates, so a later synthesis stage picks up the reduced decomposition automatically. Under simulation, the rewrite is a no-op on the state: [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") is *validate-then-rotate* (it validates the reference occupation and then applies the rotation, just as the two separate gates do), so the merge unlocks the cheaper synthesis without changing the prepared state.\n"
msgstr "Il transpiler pass [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") rileva lo schema [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") seguito da [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") in un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") e lo riscrive in gate [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), in modo che una successiva fase di sintesi sfrutti automaticamente la decomposizione ridotta. In simulazione, la riscrittura non modifica lo stato: [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") è *validate-then-rotate* (convalida l'occupazione di riferimento e poi applica la rotazione, proprio come fanno i due gate separati), quindi la fusione abilita la sintesi più economica senza cambiare lo stato preparato.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Throughout this guide, each circuit is drawn before and after the pass, side by side: the input on the left, and the result of running the pass on it on the right. Two helpers do that. `merge` runs the pass on a copy of the circuit (through its [`FermionicDAGCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-dag-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit\")) and converts the result back to a drawable [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\"), and `draw_merge` draws both halves into a single before/after figure:\n"
msgstr "In questa guida ogni circuito è disegnato prima e dopo il pass, affiancati: l'input a sinistra e, a destra, il risultato dell'esecuzione del pass su di esso. Due funzioni di supporto si occupano di questo. `merge` esegue il pass su una copia del circuito (tramite il suo [`FermionicDAGCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-dag-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicDAGCircuit\")) e converte il risultato in un [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") disegnabile, e `draw_merge` disegna entrambe le metà in un'unica figura prima/dopo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What gets merged {#what-gets-merged}"
msgstr "Che cosa viene fuso {#what-gets-merged}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pass recognizes three patterns, all keyed off the block-spin mode convention that [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") and [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") use. For a system with `norb` spatial orbitals, the modes `0..norb` are the spin-alpha sector, and `norb..2*norb` are the spin-beta sector. Slater determinant preparation is done per spin sector because each sector has its own (electrons, orbitals) shape.\n"
msgstr "Il pass riconosce tre schemi, tutti basati sulla convenzione dei modi a blocchi di spin usata da [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") e [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\"). Per un sistema con `norb` orbitali spaziali, i modi `0..norb` sono il settore di spin alfa e `norb..2*norb` sono il settore di spin beta. La preparazione del determinante di Slater viene eseguita per settore di spin perché ogni settore ha una propria forma (elettroni, orbitali).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full-register (or spinless) {#full-register-or-spinless}"
msgstr "Registro completo (o senza spin) {#full-register-or-spinless}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplest pattern is using [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), immediately followed by an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") on the *same* modes. This is the spinless case (one determinant over all modes) and also a spinful circuit whose rotation spans both sectors at once. The two gates fuse into a single [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"):\n"
msgstr "Lo schema più semplice è l'uso di [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\"), seguito immediatamente da un [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") sugli *stessi* modi. È il caso senza spin (un determinante su tutti i modi) e anche quello di un circuito con spin la cui rotazione copre entrambi i settori contemporaneamente. I due gate si fondono in un unico [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"):\n"

